        "problem": "$\\int (4x-1){e}^{2{x}^{2}-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=2{x}^{2}-x.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x-1\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}u=(4x-1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4x-1){e}^{2{x}^{2}-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{2{x}^{2}-x}\\cdot (4x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{2{x}^{2}-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
